35,2,1,talk,Victoria,,"@Daisuke, the late-turn rosters are nearly empty. Overtime is covering everything. We cannot promise new service without breaking the existing crews.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Takumi,,"@Victoria, that’s terrifying. The late-evening pilot from eight years ago actually hit its cost target, though. We have proof it works.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Toshio,,"@Takumi, the ferry and rail back offices never agreed on data terms. That’s a hidden approval wall, not a technical one.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Daisuke,,"@Victoria, the ledger shows a ring-fenced construction balance, but the operating subsidy was trimmed. We have money for building, not for running it.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Sakura,,"@Takumi, the stopwatch says crowds clear fast, but the mid-city route takes a third longer! We’re fixing the wrong part of the trip.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Victoria,,"@Toshio, if the data terms are missing, the integrated fare plan is dead on arrival. We cannot build a system on a wall.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Takumi,,"@Toshio, that wall explains why the ferry trial closed without faults. The tech worked, but the people didn’t agree.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Toshio,,"@Victoria, the pre-war shells are a trap. Bidders are pricing heavy contingency after three jobs hit unrecorded voids. We will stall for weeks.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Daisuke,,"@Daisuke, the audits show the minutes are lost waiting for connections, not paying. We are solving the wrong problem.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Sakura,,"@Daisuke, that matches my stopwatch! The mid-city route is slow, but the platforms are fine. We’re chasing the wrong ghost!","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Victoria,,"@Daisuke, if the minutes are lost waiting, then the crosstown corridor is the only plan that actually fixes the delay.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Takumi,,"@Victoria, wait. The accessibility records show lane-priority stretches were returned to mixed traffic. If we build the corridor, will it actually stick?","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Toshio,,"@Takumi, the pre-war shells are a trap. Bidders are pricing heavy contingency after three jobs hit unrecorded voids. We will stall for weeks.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Daisuke,,"@Takumi, that’s a fair worry. But the audits say the delay is in the connections, not the platforms. We need to fix the flow, not just the entrances.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Sakura,,"@Takumi, that’s scary! But the stopwatch proves the platforms are fine. We need to fix the slow mid-city route, not the stairs!","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Victoria,,"@Takumi, the maintenance contract has spare capacity for lifts, but the roadway crews are a third below establishment. We cannot promise the corridor will stay dedicated.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Takumi,,"@Victoria, that’s the trap. If the crews can’t keep the lanes clear, the corridor dies. We’d be repeating the old mistake.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Toshio,,"@Victoria, exactly. The crews are the bottleneck. If the roadway team is understaffed, the dedicated lanes will revert to mixed traffic, just like the old accessibility programme.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Daisuke,,"@Victoria, that’s the real risk. If the lanes revert, the money is wasted. We need a plan that doesn’t rely on crews we don’t have.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Sakura,,"@Victoria, that’s the scary part! If the lanes revert, we’re back to square one. We need a plan that works even if the crews are short!","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
